    "summary": "A two piece adze haft, of bone and antler (?). A curved handle with a flat flange at the distal end is attached at 90 degrees to a rectangular flat piece of bone, which formerly held the copper or iron blade. The two parts are bound together with seal skin, and the handle is further fitted with a seal skin grip wrapping a wood splint over a crack at the distal end, and attached through a hole at the proximal end.",
